  <b:collaboration id="Collaboration">
    <b:participant id="Pool" name="AscTile kernel development" processRef="Workflow" />
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0fwizfb">
      <b:text>July: pyasc-codegen-workflow/SKILL.md, Phase 1 step 2, requires golden/kernels/abs_f16.py and, if available, the upstream asc2/test_vadd.py. November: start with reference/asctile/target/test_reduce_sum.py for row sums. Consult source matching reference/asctile/PIN.json only if the shipped tests leave a question open.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_TaskTool">
      <b:text>OpenCode example: the coordinating agent calls the native skill tool with asctile-codegen-workflow and reads the returned instructions before Phase 0.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0wvkyj6">
      <b:text>Caller is the agent or harness coordinating the run. It gathers user answers and arranges worker handoffs. Follow the arrows between lanes to see who takes over.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1hylb8w">
      <b:text>Example: FP16 rows (2,64) and (2,65) → FP32 sums (2,). Ask if tolerance is missing. Every flow node has an example in its Documentation field.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0fzfuc8">
      <b:text>“For FP16 rows of widths 64 and 65, should each row produce one FP32 sum? What absolute and relative tolerances should we use?”</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1q4kwgg">
      <b:text>Phase 0 agrees scope: if the user requests tuning, confirm the baseline and time or attempt budget. Phase 4 measures variants after correctness qualification.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0vr71f6">
      <b:text>Phase 0 exit gate. Ready: agreed contract and selected runtime identified; its import exposes jit and global_tensor. Blocked: record the missing prerequisite and diagnostic, then issue the limited report.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0xxgl7w">
      <b:text>In design.md map each case to checks: static contract, exact-runtime compile, seeded CaModel comparison at agreed tolerance, and official per-case NPU results when requested.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0ucicx8">
      <b:text>Author hands Caller the agreed case matrix, tolerance, runtime identity and preflight result. Caller checks readiness and releases the same inputs to the design task. The skill specifies no separate Phase 0 handoff file.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0hrlont">
      <b:text>Example: sum_rows(x) accepts a two-dimensional FP16 tensor and returns one FP32 sum per row. Select any flow node to read its worked example in the HTML viewer or its BPMN Documentation field.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1vg9eja">
      <b:text>Design establishes feasible tile sizes, UB bounds, tail padding and dispatch rules. For width 65, try 64 columns plus a masked tail. Compile or dry-run specializations to check feasibility; the host can select a qualified route at runtime. Revise failed plans and measure tuning variants after correctness.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0ewvl07">
      <b:text>Example: accumulate FP16 rows in FP32, using zero for padded sum lanes. Evaluate a single-tile reduction or combine per-tile partials on device for wider rows. Select using the contract, pinned API support and numerical checks.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1udldj3">
      <b:text>Start from skills/asctile-codegen-workflow/templates/kernel-template.py for the common skeleton, or reference/asctile/target/test_reduce_sum.py for a matching row-reduction pattern. Verify the import against the pinned runtime.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_13j6o2d">
      <b:text>Example: wrap a 2-D input with global_tensor, copy_in the row tile with zero padding, accumulate in the agreed precision, reduce along axis 1, then copy_out one sum per valid row.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_047kqnn">
      <b:text>Match the proposal and incumbent to their reviewed hashes and official jobs. Compare the same preserved cases, device and measurement protocol. Check every case for correctness and compare the official metric against observed timing variation.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1wfe2et">
      <b:text>Keep the incumbent when any case regresses or a comparable official gain stays within measurement noise. A 1% gain inside an observed 2% noise band is insufficient. The skill sets no universal percentage. Missing comparable official measurements follow the earlier evidence gate.</b:text>
    </b:textAnnotation>
    <b:association id="Association_1a7nnuu" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="N_p4_flow7" targetRef="TextAnnotation_1wfe2et" />
